 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511736,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Kellie makes tables and chairs. Kellie profits $20 from a table (<span data-math=\"t\">t</span>), and $10 from a chair (<span data-math=\"c\">c</span>). A table requires 15 board feet of wood, while a chair requires 4 board feet of wood. Kellie has 70 board feet available. The maximum number of tables and chairs Kellie can make in any one day is 12. The four corner points of the system are:\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1000757,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{(0, 0), (0, 12), (10, 2), (12, 0)}\">{(0, 0), (0, 12), (10, 2), (12, 0)}</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000758,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{(0, 0), (0, 12), (2, 10), (4\\tfrac{2}{3} , 0)}\">{(0, 0), (0, 12), (2, 10), (4\\tfrac{2}{3} , 0)}</span>",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000759,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"{(0, 0), (17.5, 0), (2, 10), (12, 0)}\">{(0, 0), (17.5, 0), (2, 10), (12, 0)}</span>",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response",
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Where do the boundaries of these inequalities cross?</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"t + c \\le 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"15t + 4c \\le 70\"></span></p>\n<p>Solve <span data-math=\"t + c = 12\"></span> for <i>t</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"t = 12 - c\"></span></p>\n<p>Substitute into the second boundary equations and solve for <i>b</i>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"15\\left( {12 - c} \\right) + 4c = 70\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"180 - 15c + 4c = 70\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 11c =  - 110\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"c = 10\"></span></p>\n<p>Substitute into the first equation to find <i>b.</i></p>\n<p><i><span data-math=\"t = 12 - 10\"></span></i></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"t = 2\"></span></p>\n<p>The corners of the shaded area are</p>\n<ul>\n<li>the intersection of the two boundary lines: (2, 10)</li>\n<li>the points where two of the boundary lines intersect the axes: <span data-math=\"\\left( {0,12} \\right)\"></span>, and <span data-math=\"\\left( {4.\\frac{2}{3},0} \\right)\"></span></li>\n<li>(0, 0).</li>\n</ul>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
